# JSDoc function comments

Every exported function needs a **definition** (what it does), not only `@param` / `@returns`.

## Simple functions

One short definition line, then `@param` / `@returns`:

```javascript
/**
 * Normalize and deduplicate email addresses (trimmed, lowercased).
 *
 * @param {string[]} emails
 * @returns {string[]}
 */
export const dedupeEmails = (emails) => { ... };
```

## Complex functions

Add a short definition (1–2 sentences) before `@param`:

```javascript
/**
 * Build who receives notification emails based on actor role.
 * Admin actors get audit recipients only; others also get self and stakeholders.
 *
 * @param {{ actor?: object, selfEmail?: string, ... }} params
 * @returns {{ adminAudit: string[], self: string[], stakeholders: string[] }}
 */
```

## Rules

- Always include a definition line — never `@param`-only blocks
- Keep simple helpers to one line; use 1–2 sentences when behavior or routing is non-obvious
- Add `@returns` when the return value is not obvious from the definition
